Actually, you have to replace a lot more than the Konqueor package.  You have 
to replace a good deal of the underlying kde libs as well -- with ones 
compiled with -mieee.

If you are interested, see the earlier thread about SIGFPE and -mieee.

The real joy comes when you try to recompile the KDE libs with -mieee.  
Dpkg-buildpackage runs into some problems with the KDE metaclass class stuff 
and you have to manually assist the whole process along.  *grin*

Later  -T

PS:  I intend to get a GCC patch to make -mieee the default for Alpha linux 
out the door someday soon.  That way the next maintainer build of the KDE 
stuff will be good to go.

PPS:  If you want to try rebuilding the base libraries, the Konqueor 
libraries, etc (whatever all else it depends on) with -mieee, check the 
Debian KDE maillist.  I believe I posted an email about what you have to do 
to get around the KDE metaclass build problems.  

