> 
> You are probabely right...
> I will have to build my own kernel with DAC960 as a module, because the
> kernel from the install cd doesn't have de required devices but has the
> drivers not in module !
> 
> Or is there something I can restart to help the driver find the devices?
> 
> Pierre.
> 

As far as I know the standard kernel doesn't have DAC960 support built 
in, so you need to compile your own kernel. There should be no problems 
if you compile the driver directly into the kernel. This way you will 
see if your controller is recognized at boottime.

